# Biohub V1284 ablation resume — dependency-isolated v2

This runner resumes the same V1284 candidate-vs-zero causal experiment after the prior AWS run stopped before inference because `tracksdata` was absent from the canonical project `.venv`.

Changes are environment-only:
- the project `.venv` is not modified;
- public-notebook dependency recovery installs into a persistent `runtime_overlay` under the existing V1284 state root using `PIP_TARGET`;
- public child prediction processes preserve that overlay in `PYTHONPATH`;
- source bytes, model weights, thresholds, graph logic, V1284 candidate/zero intervention, and parity gates are unchanged;
- the head-ON graph must still exactly reproduce the already downloaded public 0.953 output before the ablation is interpreted.

No model fitting, Kaggle submission, Git write, or AWS infrastructure mutation is implemented.

